    <title>Cedar Trace ILS investors may provide capital to support 2027 Lloyd’s syndicate launch</title>
    <link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/cedar-trace-ils-investors-may-provide-capital-to-support-2027-lloyds-syndicate-launch/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=cedar-trace-ils-investors-may-provide-capital-to-support-2027-lloyds-syndicate-launch</link>
    <description>Investors backing insurance-linked securities funds under the management of Cedar Trace Capital Management are expected to provide some of the capital to support the planned launch of a $300m Lloyd’s syndicate for the 2027 underwriting year, by group company Cedar Trace Underwriting. Holden added, “Lloyd’s is obviously a market that David and I know extremely well and the capital and licensing advantages that it brings allow us to expand our offerings to our existing reinsurance relationships and to bring new delegated coverholders to the market.” Lorraine Harfitt, CEO, Asta, who will provide managing agency and associated services to the syndicate, stated, “We are delighted to support Cedar Trace as it establishes its Lloyd’s platform. Existing shareholders of affiliated insurer Mereo Insurance is expected to be the main source of capital to support the Cedar Trace Underwriting syndicate at Lloyd’s.</description>
