    <title>‘Physical economy is back’ as data centres become strategic infrastructure: Swiss Re</title>
    <link>https://www.reinsurancene.ws/physical-economy-is-back-as-data-centres-become-strategic-infrastructure-swiss-re/</link>
    <description>Jérôme Haegeli, Group Chief Economist at Swiss Re and Head of the Swiss Re Institute, has said the “physical economy is back” as the rapid expansion of data centre investment fuels a new global capital expenditure (capex) super-cycle. Swiss Re has said that this investment boom, spanning data centres, energy systems and other strategic infrastructure, could create one of the largest commercial property and casualty (P&amp;C) insurance opportunities in decades . Swiss Re said these investments are transforming data centres from traditional information technology assets into strategic infrastructure, with power requirements measured in gigawatts and asset values running into billions of dollars.</description>
