    <description>(Image source: IIR.) Mercury Insurance (Los Angeles) is encouraging homeowners to review wildfire mitigation improvements and consult their insurance agents about discounts that may be available. Mercury says qualifying homeowners may be eligible for wildfire mitigation discounts in multiple states where the insurer writes homeowners coverage. In California, qualifying Mercury customers may receive discounts based on measures such as defensible space, home hardening, IBHS Wildfire Prepared Home certification, qualifying community mitigation and certain types of fire-resistive construction.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:40 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://iireporter.com/mercury-highlights-wildfire-mitigation-discounts/</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Bamboo Launches Texas Homeowners Program</title>
    <link>https://iireporter.com/bamboo-launches-texas-homeowners-program/</link>
    <description>(Image source: IIR.) Bamboo Insurance (Midvale, Utah) has launched its Texas Essential Homeowner Program, an admitted homeowners product designed to give policyholders more flexibility in structuring coverage. The program is intended to provide an alternative for Texas homeowners facing rising renewal costs from traditional carriers, according to a Bamboo statement. Expanding Essential Homeowners Program The Texas launch follows Bamboo’s July introduction of its Essential homeowners program in California and a relationship with MS Transverse that added about $150 million of admitted capacity in that state.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:39 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://iireporter.com/bamboo-launches-texas-homeowners-program/</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Applied Targets Benefits Workflow Fragmentation</title>
    <link>https://iireporter.com/applied-targets-benefits-workflow-fragmentation/</link>
    <description>(Image source: IIR.) Applied Systems’ expansion of its Employee Navigator integration addresses one of the most persistent inefficiencies in employee benefits: entering the same plan information repeatedly as it moves among quoting, agency management and enrollment systems. The newly expanded integration lets brokers transfer finalized benefits plan data directly from Applied Epic to Employee Navigator. The development is more than an improvement to an existing connection, according to Tammi Shapiro, SVP and General Manager, Benefits Solutions, Applied Systems (Chicago).</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:15:39 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://iireporter.com/applied-targets-benefits-workflow-fragmentation/</guid>
    <category>General</category>
