  <item>
    <title>Brazil’s growing LRS market broadens the range of risks available to ILS capital: Pereira, Santé</title>
    <link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/brazils-growing-lrs-market-broadens-the-range-of-risks-available-to-ils-capital-pereira-sante/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=brazils-growing-lrs-market-broadens-the-range-of-risks-available-to-ils-capital-pereira-sante</link>
    <description>With activity picking up in Brazil’s ILS market and an increasing number of Brazilian Letra de Risco de Seguro (LRS) transactions completing, Pereira, recently spoke to Artemis to discuss how Brazil’s LRS instrument can help broaden the range of risks available to ILS investors. Brazil’s developing insurance-linked securities (ILS) market could create a clear route for catastrophe exposures that historically have remained uninsured or concentrated on traditional balance sheets to access institutional capital, Mirelle Pereira, founder of risk intelligence company Santé told Artemis. Four LRS transactions had been completed by May 2026, including a R$126 million issuance by Galápagos Capital SSPE, the largest under the regime at the time,” Pereira told Artemis.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:33:29 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.artemis.bm/news/brazils-growing-lrs-market-broadens-the-range-of-risks-available-to-ils-capital-pereira-sante/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=brazils-growing-lrs-market-broadens-the-range-of-risks-available-to-ils-capital-pereira-sante</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Strong ILS demand and continued growth expected at year-end and in 2027: Pennay, Aon</title>
    <link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/strong-ils-demand-and-continued-growth-expected-at-year-end-and-in-2027-pennay-aon/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=strong-ils-demand-and-continued-growth-expected-at-year-end-and-in-2027-pennay-aon</link>
    <description>The insurance-linked securities (ILS) market will see strong demand through the end of 2026 and into 2027, while the asset class is also likely to grow further with catastrophe bonds and sidecars key areas as cedents integrate ILS products into their reinsurance, according to Richard Pennay, CEO of Aon Securities. Facilitating these reinsurance partnership’s, Pennay said that Aon works with its clients to “ultimately form a view as to how ILS can complement those structures.” Pennay continued to explain, “In addition to that demand from our clients, we are seeing an overwhelming supply of capacity from the insurance-linked securities investors. “The ILS market today is truly at its strongest stance that it has ever been over the 20 plus year evolution of this market,” Pennay explained, “We certainly have the sense that that this market is at its strongest point today.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:33:29 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.artemis.bm/news/strong-ils-demand-and-continued-growth-expected-at-year-end-and-in-2027-pennay-aon/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=strong-ils-demand-and-continued-growth-expected-at-year-end-and-in-2027-pennay-aon</guid>
    <category>General</category>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Still early for casualty sidecars, but growing investor appetite pressures reinsurance pricing: Fitch</title>
    <link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/still-early-for-casualty-sidecars-but-growing-investor-appetite-pressures-reinsurance-pricing-fitch/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=still-early-for-casualty-sidecars-but-growing-investor-appetite-pressures-reinsurance-pricing-fitch</link>
    <description>During Fitch Ratings’ 2027 Global Reinsurance Outlook webinar, just in advance of the Monte Carlo Rendez-vous event, Schneider outlined expected pricing trends for casualty lines as the industry moves toward year-end renewals, noting a clear market split. In a report published by Fitch earlier this year, the agency highlighted how the reinsurance sidecar market witnessed rapid growth in 2025, particularly in Bermuda, where a number of major re/insurers launched casualty reinsurance sidecars during the year. Speaking this week, Fitch Ratings’ Senior Director, NA, Brian Schneider highlighted that as capital flows into the space, the additional supply is putting added pressure on casualty pricing.</description>
    <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:33:29 +0000</pubDate>
    <guid>https://www.artemis.bm/news/still-early-for-casualty-sidecars-but-growing-investor-appetite-pressures-reinsurance-pricing-fitch/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=still-early-for-casualty-sidecars-but-growing-investor-appetite-pressures-reinsurance-pricing-fitch</guid>
